# BK-0011M BOS ROM, 140000-157777. System-call names come from common.ann.
# Section comments are from reading the code, checked against the BOS
# manual 00015-01.32.01 where it says something about the same thing.

code 140000 RESET ; power-on entry: the VM1 starts at SEL1's high byte, 140000
head 140000 Power-on: mask interrupts and go to the cold start.

ptrs 140010 134
head 140010 System call table (BOS manual §2.3): one slot per EMT 0-133.
head 140010 JSR PC,@slot calls a routine directly; EMT n goes through EMTDSP.

code 140300 COLD
head 140300 Cold start. Stack at 1000; system RAM page 7 at 040000 and ROM
head 140300 page 1 at 100000; set up low memory (INIVEC); print the banner
head 140300 (BANNER, in ROM page 1) and scroll it up the screen.
note 140370 user mapping copy: 040000 = RAM page 5 (screen 0), 100000 = RAM page 4
note 140376 key held down at power-on?
note 140404 yes: skip booting, go to the monitor
note 140406 floppy controller found?
note 140414 .BABOOT: boot from floppy
head 140420 Scan ROM pages 3, 2, 1, 0 (R0 = 413 down to 410). For each page that
head 140420 exists, call 120000 if it answers, then 100000 if it answers. Page 1
head 140420 is only called if it starts with NOP (000240), the autostart marker
head 140420 that BASIC page 1 carries. Vector 4 catches missing ROMs meanwhile.

code 140562 MONENT
head 140562 Enter the keyboard monitor.

code 140576 TRAP4 ; default handler for vector 4 and all unused vectors
head 140576 Catch-all trap handler (INIVEC points vectors 4-376 here). SEL1
head 140576 bit 2 is set by HALT and the STOP key but not by a bus error
head 140576 (BOS manual §1.3): HALT/STOP go to the monitor, a bus error goes
head 140576 to the user's .BTRPS handler if one is set. Leaves with RTT.
note 140602 save SEL1: bit 2 = HALT or STOP rather than a bus error

code 140712 MONITR
head 140712 Keyboard monitor: take over vector 4, save the interrupted PC and
head 140712 PSW, then continue in ROM page 1 at 120002 (MONMAI).

code 150170 INIVEC
head 150170 Set up low memory: JMP @#BEXIT at address 0, so a jump to 0 returns
head 150170 to the monitor; every vector 4-376 -> TRAP4 at PSW 2341. Vectors 100
head 150170 and 274 point at their own PSW word, which holds 000002 (RTI), so
head 150170 they return at once until a driver installs a real handler.
note 150176 address 0: JMP @#BEXIT
note 150232 vector 100 -> 102, which holds RTI
note 150254 vector 274 -> 276, which holds RTI

code 152112 EMTDSP
head 152112 EMT dispatcher. The low byte of the EMT instruction picks a slot in
head 152112 the system call table (EMT 0-133). The caller's C flag is passed in,
head 152112 and the routine's C flag passed back, through the saved PSW. Larger
head 152112 EMT numbers go to the user's handler in EMTUSR (166), or print an
head 152112 error and enter the monitor.
note 152132 caller's C flag -> C
note 152144 C -> saved PSW
